# All text stays LF — in the repo AND in every checkout, Windows included
# (overrides core.autocrlf=true defaults). Runtime code and verify fixtures
# read checked-out files with \n expectations, and every modern Windows editor
# handles LF. Binaries (fonts/images) are auto-detected and untouched.
# Verified a no-op for existing checkouts when added: the whole index was
# already LF (git ls-files --eol, 2026-07-27).
* text=auto eol=lf
# The signed add-on is committed (only the maintainer can produce one). text=auto already
# detects it as binary, but a signed archive silently corrupted by EOL conversion would be
# a miserable thing to diagnose, so say it outright.
*.xpi binary
